                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Alright. I'll be the first to admit I like this little game a little too much for what it really is! . . . But at the same time, isn't it what well-made little finds are supposed to achieve?!\n\nIn these quick head-to-head matches, you just pick a character (Marilyn, Roger Federer, or a pink 'Darth Vader', etc.) and you throw your absurd weapon (lipstick, light saber, or tennis racket, etc.) at your rival who stands on an opposing platform out in space, which is randomly located each time.\n\nIn case this doesn't scream \"stupidly awesome\" enough to you, let me add that the game is actually really well-made! It runs smoothly without issues, and the effects of the wind and gravity feel quite realistic, forcing you to smartly anticipate your strength and angle before each throw. And with winds changing each turn, here you have your nice little challenge all cut-out for you! \n\nAfter a certain point, especially after your rival hits you on the 'helmet' ([spoiler]or skull [/spoiler]) a few times, the quick back-and-forth rapidly becomes all personal and rivalries start to emerge (or long-time friendships begin to end). \n\nOf course I would love more players ('any' players for that matter) in the multiplayer rooms. And I hope the devs adjust the points (*stars*) system as it takes too long to unlock all characters (I really want my 'Money Man' aka: Lord Gaben!)\n\nBut outside of this, it's really just a nice little gem. Perfect to challenge some friends in a space-duel, or even to play at a party (maybe even as a tournament) on a single computer with anyone present and brave enough to face-off in this colorful corner of our dark universe.\n\nMay the solar winds be with you!",
